Failed to load plugins
@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-conversation
@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-cordis
failed to apply loader entry f90db188 (@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-conversation): single slot "details" already has a registration at priority 0 (registered by x6) — register at a different priority to shadow it (lowest renders)

**Package**: `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-settings-plugins`
**Environment**: DSH v0.1.0-rc.5 source checkout, Windows, reproduced with dsh-vision-router plugin
## Summary

On a fresh page load, the **Settings → Plugins → Configurable** tab shows the empty state even though third-party plugin cards (e.g. `dsh-vision-router`) are registered into the `settings.plugin.item` slot. The cards only appear after a manual page reload. The user ends up needing a refresh every time they open the settings page for the first time.

## Root cause

`ConfigurablePluginsTab` decides between the empty state and rendering cards based on a **one-time mount-time snapshot** of the slot ledger:

```tsx
// packages/client/ui-settings-plugins/src/client/ConfigurablePluginsTab.tsx
export function ConfigurablePluginsTab({ t, renderSlot, cardCount }: ConfigurablePluginsTabProps) {
  return cardCount === 0
    ? <p className={css.empty}>{t('empty')}</p>
    : <ul className={css.cards}>{renderSlot('settings.plugin.item', {})}</ul>
}
```

The snapshot comes from the tab registration's inject, which reads the ledger **once at mount** and never subscribes:

```ts
// packages/client/ui-settings-plugins/src/client/index.ts
ctx.slots.inject('settings.plugins.tab', () => ctx.slots.register({
  name: 'settings.plugins.tab',
  id: 'configurable',
  order: 0,
  label: () => t('configurableTab'),
  locale: NS,
  inject: (): ConfigurablePluginsTabInjected => ({
    cardCount: ctx.slots.entries('settings.plugin.item').length, // ← static mount-time snapshot
  }),
  children: { 'settings.plugin.item': { kind: 'list', scope: 'root' } },
}, ConfigurablePluginsTab))
```

When the browser opens the settings page before a plugin's client bundle has finished loading (a startup race between bundles), `cardCount` snapshots to `0`. Because the value is static and never subscribed, the component keeps rendering the empty state **forever** — even after the plugin's card registers into the slot moments later. `renderSlot` is reactive, but it is never reached while `cardCount === 0`.

## Why the three built-in cards never hit this

The built-in cards (`bash`, `agent-loop`, `web-search`) are registered in the **same** `apply()` run, after the tab registration — so by the time the tab mounts, its snapshot already counts them. Only **external plugins** that register their cards from a separately-loaded bundle are subject to the race, which is why this goes unnoticed in first-party testing.

## Proposed fix

Make `cardCount` reactive, mirroring the existing `tabs` hook pattern in the same file (`sectionInjected` already uses `getSnapshot` + `subscribe` on the slot ledger).

```ts
// index.ts
inject: (): ConfigurablePluginsTabInjected => ({
  hooks: {
    cardCount: {
      getSnapshot: () => ctx.slots.entries('settings.plugin.item').length,
      subscribe: (listener: () => void) => ctx.slots.subscribe('settings.plugin.item', listener),
    },
  },
}),
```

```tsx
// ConfigurablePluginsTab.tsx
export interface ConfigurablePluginsTabInjected {
  hooks: {
    cardCount: HostObservable<number>
  }
}

export function ConfigurablePluginsTab({ t, renderSlot, useCardCount }: ConfigurablePluginsTabProps) {
  const cardCount = useCardCount(value => value)
  return cardCount === 0
    ? <p className={css.empty}>{t('empty')}</p>
    : <ul className={css.cards}>{renderSlot('settings.plugin.item', {})}</ul>
}
```

(`HostObservable` is already exported from `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-slots` and used by `PluginsSettingsSection`.)

## Verification

With the fix, on a fresh page load the plugin card appears as soon as its bundle registers — no manual refresh needed. Verified locally with `dsh-vision-router` (which registers a card into `settings.plugin.item`).

## Related

The race also explains a user-facing workaround floating around the community: "reload the page once and the card appears" — that works only because a reload remounts the tab after the plugin bundle has already loaded.

## Bug description

On Windows, the native directory picker (`IFileOpenDialog` driven via koffi in a spawned worker) **truncates the selected path at any character whose code point is a multiple of 0x100** (low byte `0x00` in UTF-16LE). Selecting e.g.

```
C:\Users\Starry\OneDrive\Desktop\agent周事项\剪切板工具开发
```

is returned as

```
C:\Users\Starry\OneDrive\Desktop\agent周事项\剪切板工具
```

Everything from 开 (U+5F00) onward is cut off, so creating a workspace on such a folder fails with `workspace-invalid-path: ENOENT` (the backend receives a path that does not exist).

## Environment
- OS: Windows 10/11
- `@deepseek-ai/dsh` / `@deepseek-ai/dsh-host-directory-picker-native`: 0.1.0-rc.6
- 100% reproducible, not input-related

## Root cause

`readUtf16` in `packages/host/directory-picker-native/src/win32-dialog-bindings.ts` (built artifact `lib/worker.cjs`) finds the NUL terminator by testing only the even-offset (low) byte:

```js
function readUtf16(koffi, address) {
  const bytes = Buffer.from(koffi.view(address, 32768));
  let end = 0;
  while (end + 1 < bytes.length && bytes[end] !== 0) end += 2;
  return bytes.toString("utf16le", 0, end);
}
```

A UTF-16LE terminator is two zero bytes (`00 00`), but the loop stops at a single zero byte. Any character with `codePoint % 0x100 === 0` has a zero low byte — e.g. 开 U+5F00 encodes as `00 5F`, 一 U+4E00 as `00 4E` — and is mistaken for the terminator, truncating the rest of the string. ASCII is unaffected (its zero byte sits at odd offsets).

## Proposed fix

```js
function readUtf16(koffi, address) {
  const bytes = Buffer.from(koffi.view(address, 32768));
  let end = 0;
  while (end + 1 < bytes.length && !(bytes[end] === 0 && bytes[end + 1] === 0)) end += 2;
  return bytes.toString("utf16le", 0, end);
}
```

Verified against several CJK paths (开发 / 一 / 签字单); all decode completely.

## Notes
- Affects any path containing a U+XX00 character (开, 一, …), not just this example.
- Workaround: patch the condition in `lib/worker.cjs`; the worker is spawned per pick, so no restart is required (the local node_modules patch is overwritten on upgrade).

